From 3740edc5949ff154fcd8f96ff33301077885646f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:42:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] VC3D: Rotate/Flip Apply saves only over the geometry it
 transformed

When Rotate opens it records the geometry revision of the surface it
transforms: the one the segment's store edit holds for it (opened at or
last saved as), no longer the store head. Apply passes it to
SegmentationModule::saveSurface, and SurfaceStoreEdit::save refuses the
write unless the edit still holds that geometry revision. The check runs
under the edit's lock after a pending save is resolved and after
saveSurface has waited for a running autosave, so a save that finishes
during Apply is kept instead of overwritten.

When Apply is cancelled or refused because a newer geometry revision is
stored while the tool's source is still the active surface, the tool
reopens the segment through the surface panel (and deselects it only if
that fails). The next Rotate, the panel and the agent bridge then start
from the saved geometry: after the panel's Flip saved during a pending
Apply, Rotate opens again on the flipped segment, and a retry after an
autosave of the shown preview starts from that autosave.

A revision lookup that returns nothing never matches: Apply saves
nothing, and the segment stays selected because nothing newer is known.
CWindow's stored-revision reader returns the head's geometry revision,
the kind of revision the store edit holds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
